 ## Unreleased — 1.4.0
 
-Nothing yet.
+### `fmt` no longer re-parses what it just wrote
+
+`cmd_fmt` re-parsed its own formatted output and refused to emit anything whose records or
+labels moved on the way back through. The guard never had a live input — it could only fire on
+a defect in `write_surface`, not on anything a user could type — so every `fmt` invocation paid
+for a second full parse of every file to check something no document could ever trip. Removed;
+the property is still pinned where it can actually break, in `crates/smysl-core/tests/surface.rs`,
+`roundtrip.rs` and `versioning.rs`. Halves the parsing work `fmt` does per file.
 
 ---
 
